  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en-US
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8ce8538dbe596345945145ec7e17596, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 2524761374326784
    m_Localized: 'Game Components

      Common Components: 1 Game Board, 30 Strategy
      Cards, Gold Bars, Gold Coins

      Components for each player: 1 Castle,
      2 Miners, 3 Pioneers, 2 Bombards, 72 Roads'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2525352641167360
    m_Localized: "Basic Setting (2-player strategy game)\r\nGame Overview\r\nThis
      game is a turn-based 2-player strategy boardgame. In this game, players deploy
      units to capture the opponent\u2019s castle. Each castle has 5 HP (Hit Points).
      You win by sending units (such as Pioneers or Bombards) to reduce the enemy
      castle's HP to 0.\r\n\r\nSetup\r\nCastles: Place each castle on its designated
      color tile.\r\nStrategy Cards: Shuffle the Strategy Cards face-down and place
      them in a draw pile.\r\nPlacement Rules: * Roads must always be placed along
      the edges of the hexagonal tiles. Similarly, Miners, Pioneers, and Bombards
      must be placed on the vertices (corners) of the hexagonal tiles.\r\n\r\nTurn
      Structure\r\nEach player follows this specific sequence during their turn:\r\nProduction
      Phase\r\nDraw Phase\r\nMain Phase\r\nEnd of Turn (Pass to the opponent)\r\nNote:
      Strategy Cards can be played at any time during your own turn, regardless of
      the current phase"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2525795303817216
    m_Localized: "Production Turn\n\nDuring the Production Turn, players gain Gold
      Bars and Gold Coins from their Castles and Producers.\n\nBy default, each Castle
      provides 2 Gold Bars, while Producers generate Gold Coins depending on the
      types of tiles they are adjacent to.\nEvery 5 Gold Coins are automatically
      converted into 1 Gold Bar.\n(5 Gold Coins = 1 Gold Bar)\n\nA Producer earns
      Gold Coins equal to the production value of the tile type it is most strongly
      connected to among adjacent tiles.\nEach tile has a different production value:\n\nThe
      amount of Gold Coins gained depends on the tile color\nDarker tiles yield higher
      production\n\nHowever, there are cases where a Producer cannot generate Gold
      Coins:\n\nWhen the opponent has used a \u201CDrought\u201D card\nWhen the Producer
      is not connected to the Castle via a Sanctuary and Road\n\nIn the Production
      Turn:\n\nThe 2 Gold Bars from the Castle must always be collected\nCastle production
      is not affected by \u201CDrought\u201D\n\nHowever:\n\nA player can hold a maximum
      of 20 Gold Bars\nIf this limit is exceeded, no additional Gold Bars can be
      gained during the Production Turn\n\nAdditionally, to compensate for the disadvantage
      of going second:\n\nThe second player gains 3 Gold Bars (instead of 2) from
      their Castle only during their first Production Turn"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2527252967063552
    m_Localized: "Draw Phase\r\nThe Draw Phase is when players may purchase Strategy
      Cards to gain tactical advantages.\r\nCost: Each card costs 2 Gold Bars. You
      can only purchase 1 card per turn.\r\nHand Limit: You may hold a maximum of
      5 Strategy Cards.\r\nVisibility: Strategy Cards must be kept face-down in a
      visible area so your opponent can see how many cards you currently hold.\r\nUsage
      Rules:\r\nYou may only use one card of the same name per turn (with the exception
      of Firepower).\r\nUsed cards are placed in the face-up discard pile.\r\nSpecial
      Rule (Fortify): This card is \"one-time use\" only. Once played, it is removed
      from the game entirely rather than discarded.\r\nReshuffling: If the draw pile
      is empty, shuffle the face-up discard pile and place it face-down to form a
      new draw pile.\r\n\nStrategy Cards (Total: 30 Cards)\r\nThere are 5 unique
      types of cards in the deck:\r\nFortify (Qty: 1)\r\nReinforce your walls to
      increase your Castle\u2019s HP by 1. (Removed from the game after use).\r\nDrought
      (Qty: 4)\r\nYour opponent cannot collect production from their Miners on their
      next turn. (Does not affect Castle production).\r\nProsperity (Qty: 4)\r\nImmediately
      gain 4 Gold Bars. This card can be played even if a \"Drought\" card was used
      against you.\r\nModify Road (Qty: 6)\r\nSelect and change one of your opponent's
      roads that is connected to your own road.\r\nFirepower (Qty: 15)\r\nAllows
      a Bombard to perform a ranged attack or defend against an incoming enemy Bombard
      attack."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2527682799337472
    m_Localized: "Main Phase\r\nThe Main Phase is where you build roads, recruit
      units, move, and attack.\r\n1. Road Construction & Costs\r\nFree Roads: You
      receive 2 Roads for free at the start of your turn. These must be used in this
      turn or they will vanish.\r\nRecruitment Costs:\r\nMiner: 1 Gold Bar\r\nPioneer:
      3 Gold Bars\r\nBombard: 5 Gold Bars\r\nRoad Connectivity: * Roads can only
      be extended if they are connected to your Castle.\r\nIf a road segment is cut
      off from the Castle, you can still move across it, but you cannot build new
      roads from it.\r\nIf there are no valid empty edges left on the board, no more
      roads can be built.\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Unit Deployment (Spawning)\r\nLocation: Units
      must be spawned on a vertex (corner) of your Castle's starting tile.\r\nLimit:
      You may spawn only one unit per turn.\r\nRestrictions: * Only one unit can
      occupy a single vertex.\r\nAlso you cannot spawn a unit on a vertex that is
      directly adjacent (one space away) to an enemy unit.\r\n\r\n3. Movement Rules\r\nAfter
      spawning, you may choose one Miner, one Pioneer, and one Bombard already on
      the board to move and attack. You must choose one of the two following methods:\r\nMethod
      A (Off-Road): * Pioneers can always move 1 space.\r\nMiners and Bombards can
      move 1 space only if there is no enemy road on that path.\r\nMethod B (On-Road):
      All units can travel any distance in a single move as long as they stay on
      a continuous line of your own connected roads.\r\nNote: Units cannot move a
      second time after their initial action. \r\n\r\n4. Unit Abilities & Combat\r\nMiner\r\nSpecialty:
      Focused on production; cannot attack.\r\nSupply Line: Must be connected to
      the Castle via a road to generate Gold Coins.\r\nPioneer\r\nMelee Attack: Moves
      into an enemy's space to destroy their unit.\r\nSpecial Ability (Road Capture):
      When a Pioneer moves or attacks, all roads touching its new position immediately
      change to your color.\r\nBombard\r\nMelee Attack: Moves into an enemy's space
      to destroy them (like a Pioneer).\r\nRanged Attack: Can attack an enemy 1 space
      away by consuming 1 Firepower Card.\r\nArtillery Duel: Bombards must use Ranged
      Attacks to fight other Bombards. If the defender also plays a Firepower card,
      it is a Draw (cards are spent, but both units survive). If the defender has
      no card, their Bombard is destroyed.\r\nCombo: A Bombard can perform a Melee
      Attack and then immediately follow up with a Ranged Attack in the same turn.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n5.
      Attacking the Castle\r\nSuccess in attacking a Castle reduces its HP and requires
      strategic sacrifice.\r\nPioneer Attack: Reaching a vertex of the enemy Castle
      tile reduces Castle HP by 1.\r\nBombard Attack: * Melee: Reaching the Castle
      vertex reduces Castle HP by 2.\r\nRanged: Using 1 Firepower card from 1 space
      away reduces Castle HP by 2.\r\nThe Sacrifice: Any unit that successfully damages
      the enemy Castle is permanently removed from the game and cannot be respawned."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
